# 19. The Central Theoretical Proposition

The architecture can be summarized by the following proposed principle.

### Relational Mathematical Synthesis Principle

> **A mathematical problem can be represented as a state embedded within a structured relational space of mathematical objects and transformations. A valid solution can then be synthesized as an optimized trajectory through that space, subject to immutable mathematical constraints, and compiled into an executable program.**

Formally:

[
\boxed{
\mathcal S:
(q,\mathcal V_t,\mathcal C)
\rightarrow
P^*
}
]

where:

[
P^*
===

\arg\min_{P\models\mathcal C}
J(P).
]

The resulting executable program interacts with the environment and produces new information:

[
\boxed{
P^*(W_t)\rightarrow W_{t+1}
}
]

which subsequently modifies the learned relationship structure:

[
\boxed{
\mathcal R_t\rightarrow\mathcal R_{t+1}.
}
]

